     "text": "```python\nclass Library:\n    \"\"\"\n    A class representing a library that can add and remove books.\n    It maintains a collection of books and provides methods to manage them.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes a new instance of the Library class.\n        The library starts with an empty collection of books.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.books = []\n\n    def add_book(self, book):\n        \"\"\"\n        Adds a book to the library's collection.\n\n        Parameters:\n        book (str): The title of the book to be added.\n\n        Raises:\n        ValueError: If the book is already in the collection.\n        \"\"\"\n        if book in self.books:\n            raise ValueError(\"Book already exists in the library.\")\n        self.books.append(book)\n\n    def remove_book(self, book):\n        \"\"\"\n        Removes a book from the library's collection.\n\n        Parameters:\n        book (str): The title of the book to be removed.\n\n        Raises:\n        ValueError: If the book is not in the library's collection.\n        \"\"\"\n        if book not in self.books:\n            raise ValueError(\"Book not found in the library.\")\n        self.books.remove(book)\n```",
